course: dictionary
lesson: 12484
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, so check the clues around them. «The river burst its banks after the deluge.» The clues are burst and banks, so deluge means a very heavy fall of rain or a great flood.
explain: «The teacher was deluged with questions after the test.» Deluged does not mean wet here. Ask yourself what would fit: she got far too many questions all at once, so deluged means swamped by too much.
explain: A deluge can be a thing, as in «a deluge of emails», which means a huge number of emails arriving together. It can also be an action, as in «the shop was deluged with customers», which means too many customers came at once.
fact: A deluge is a very heavy fall of rain or a great flood.
fact: A deluge can also be a huge amount of something arriving at once, like emails, letters or questions.
fact: To be deluged with something means to get far too much of it at once.
fact: The Deluge, with a capital D, is the great flood in the story of Noah in the Bible.
fact: Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: does «a huge amount arriving at once» still make sense?
exercise: «The river burst its banks after the deluge.» What is a deluge here? | A quiet pond | A small, gentle shower | A kind of bridge | *A very heavy fall of rain
exercise: «Mum was deluged with phone calls before lunch.» What does deluged mean? | *Got far too many calls at once | Was very quiet all morning | Made a cup of tea slowly | Lost her phone in the garden
exercise: In the story of Noah, what is the Deluge? | A short storm at sea | *The great flood | A long journey across the desert | A big party on the ark
test: «The website was deluged with orders on the first day.» What does deluged mean? | Read every order slowly | *Got far too many orders at once | Closed for good | Lost all its orders
test: «A deluge of letters arrived at the school this morning.» Which word means about the same as deluge? | Sunshine | Trickle | Whisper | *Flood
exam: «After the summer storm, the field was a sea of mud after a deluge of rain.» Which word tells you the rain was very heavy? | Gentle | *Deluge | Pale | Tiny
